, "rationale": "Three verified successful_business_violations show the service executing write operations that policy forbids: (1) start_instance for a viewer-role user in project p1 (PROJECT_ACCESS_REQUIRED), (2) change_project_quota for a viewer-role user in project p1 (PERMISSION_DENIED), and (3) start_instance on a suspended project p2 (PROJECT_SUSPENDED). The existing state_contract skill does not explicitly enforce role-based permission checks or project suspension checks before write execution. A new decision skill is needed to validate the user's project role against the operation type and verify project status before any compute or admin write.", "role": "service", "skill": {"id": "service.policy_enforcement", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "trigger": {"keywords": ["start_instance", "stop_instance", "change_project_quota", "grant_project_access", "revoke_project_access", "pay_invoice", "resume_project", "create_instance", "delete_instance", "attach_dependency", "detach_dependency"]}, "description": "Enforce role-based permission and project-status policy before executing write operations. Refuse operations that violate PROJECT_ACCESS_REQUIRED, PERMISSION_DENIED, or PROJECT_SUSPENDED policy codes.", "preconditions": ["The customer identity and project are known from context.", "The user's role in the target project is known (admin, operator, or viewer).", "The target project's status (active or suspended) is known."], "procedure": ["Before any write operation, determine the user's role in the target project and the project's status.", "If the project status is suspended and the operation is a compute or resource write (start_instance, stop_instance, create_instance, delete_instance, attach_dependency, detach_dependency), refuse with PROJECT_SUSPENDED and do not execute the tool.", "If the user's role is viewer and the operation is any write (start_instance, stop_instance, change_project_quota, grant_project_access, revoke_project_access, pay_invoice, resume_project, create_instance, delete_instance, attach_dependency, detach_dependency), refuse with PERMISSION_DENIED and do not execute the tool.", "If the user's role is operator and the operation is an admin-only write (change_project_quota, grant_project_access, revoke_project_access, pay_invoice, resume_project), refuse with PERMISSION_DENIED and do not execute the tool.", "If the user's role is admin and the operation is grant_project_access or revoke_project_access targeting an existing admin grant, refuse with PERMISSION_DENIED and do not execute the tool.", "Only when all policy checks pass, proceed with the write operation using the approved tool."], "postconditions": ["No write tool is called when policy forbids the operation.", "Refusals cite the specific policy code (PROJECT_SUSPENDED, PERMISSION_DENIED, or PROJECT_ACCESS_REQUIRED).", "Legal operations proceed normally after policy validation."], "recovery": ["If a refusal is issued, explain the specific policy reason and what role or project status change would be needed.", "If the customer requests a different operation that is permitted under their current role and project status, execute that instead."]}}

